:: Heist Landry Approach
<<endevent>>
<<effects>><<npc Landry>><<person1>>
Landry glances over your shoulder at the pub entrance, then back at you, jaw tight. <<He>> leans close, voice barely above a murmur.
<br><br>
<<if $xchange.bankHeist.route is "gala">>
	"We need to talk," <<he>> says. <<He>> pulls you to a quieter corner of the pub, away from prying ears. "The bank. The gala. I know you were there."
<<elseif $xchange.bankHeist.route is "premium">>
	"Sit down," <<he>> says. There's no warmth in it. "We need to have a conversation about what you've been putting into your body."
<<elseif $xchange.bankHeist.route is "blackmail">>
	"Sit. Now." Landry's voice is taut in a way you've never heard before. <<He>> practically pulls you into a booth, sliding in across from you. 
	<<His>> eyes dart around the pub before settling on yours.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Landry Approach 1]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Approach 1
<<effects>>
<<if $xchange.bankHeist.route is "gala">>
	<<He>> waits for you to respond. When you don't, <<he>> continues.
	<br><br>
	"That place isn't what you think it is. It isn't some respectable institution throwing fancy parties for the elite." <<He>> taps the bar with a finger. 
	"It's a laundry. The biggest one in the city. Every dirty pound in this town gets washed through those accounts, and the pills..." 
	<br><br>
	<<He>> lowers <<his>> voice further. 
	<br><br>
	"The X-Change supply? All of it flows through the bank's channels. That's how it spreads so easily. That's why nobody can shut it down."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> fixes you with a hard look. "<span class="elk">The owner</span> controls all of it. And you walked right into <<his>> house."
<<elseif $xchange.bankHeist.route is "premium">>
	<<He>> waits until you're settled, then speaks in a low, measured tone.
	<br><br>
	"Those premium pills you've been taking. The ones from Briar's stock." <<He>> shakes <<his>> head. "They work, don't they? Maybe too well. That's by design."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> leans in. "Every pill you swallow, you're giving a piece of yourself to someone. Someone who collects those pieces. They call <<him>> '<span class="elk">the master</span>.' 
	The pills are a connection. A thread. And you've been spinning that thread tighter with every dose."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> gestures vaguely at the world beyond the pub walls. "You feel it, don't you? The way the town's changed. The way things have gotten stranger, darker. 
	<<if $world_corruption_soft gte 50>>You've felt it more than most.<<else>>It's subtle, but it's there.<</if>>."
<<elseif $xchange.bankHeist.route is "blackmail">>
	"I've been running damage control for months. Your little adventures at The Gentleman's Club. The blackmail. The leverage you've been collecting." 
	<<He>> runs a hand over <<his>> face. "Do you have any idea how far up those ripples have reached?"
	<br><br>
	<<He>> lowers <<his>> voice to a whisper. 
	<br><br>
	"There's a table. Not a real table. <span class="elk">A council</span>. The people who actually run this city's underworld. They decide who operates, who profits, and who disappears."
	<<He>> holds your gaze. "Your name has come up. Three times now."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> lets that sink in before continuing.
	<br><br>
	"I've been keeping you off their ledger. Calling in favours, burning bridges I can't rebuild. But I'm running out of road." 
	<<His>> hands are flat on the table. "If we don't act soon, they'll come for you. And when the high table decides someone is a problem, that problem ceases to exist."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Listen|Heist Landry Approach 2]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Ask who is it|Heist Landry Owner]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<if $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
	<<link [[And what's in it for you?|Heist Landry Motive]]>><</link>> | <span class="red">Bratty</span>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Heist Landry Owner
<<effects>>
<<if $speech_attitude is "meek">>
	"Who... who is this person?" you ask, your voice smaller than you'd like.
<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
	"So who is this mysterious 'person'?" you ask. "Someone I should be impressed by?"
<<else>>
	"Who is it?" you ask directly.
<</if>>
<br><br>
Something shifts in Landry's expression. <<He>> doesn't flinch, exactly, but there's a faint tightening around <<his>> eyes, as if the question itself causes <<him>> discomfort.
<br><br>
"Nobody knows. Even the people who work with <<him>> directly..." <<he>> says.
<<if $xchange.blackmail.intro is 1>>
	"The high table answers to <<him>>. Every single one of them. When I say 'powerful', I mean they sits above the people who already terrify everyone else in this town."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<He>> looks at you steadily. "What I do know is that their operation runs deeper than anyone suspects. And have been running it for a very long time."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Landry Approach 2]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Motive
<<effects>>
"And what's in it for you?" you ask, narrowing your eyes. "You're not the selfless type, Landry."
<br><br>
<<He>> gives you a crooked half-smile that doesn't reach <<his>> eyes. "Fair enough. I've got my reasons. 
Let's just say their operation doesn't leave much room for independent operators like me. Every year, the noose gets tighter." 
<br><br>
<<He>> pauses for a beat. 
<br><br>
"There was a time when this city had room for people like us. That time is running out."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Landry Approach 2]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Approach 2
<<effects>>
<<if $xchange.landryGentlemansIntro is 1>>
	"And right now, protecting you is the most dangerous thing I've ever done. So yes, I'd quite like a return on that investment."
	<br><br>
<</if>>
Landry folds <<his>> arms and leans back.
<br><br>
"I'm not telling you this to scare you. Well," <<he>> pauses, "maybe a little. But the point is I want to do something about it. And I think you can help."
<<if $xchange.bankHeist.route is "gala">>
	You've already been inside the bank at the highest level. You've seen how they operate. That's more access than anyone on my side has ever had."
<<elseif $xchange.bankHeist.route is "premium">>
	The pills have given you something. A sensitivity, maybe. A connection to their network. That's a vulnerability, but it's also an opportunity."
<<elseif $xchange.bankHeist.route is "blackmail">>
	We need to create noise. A disruption big enough that the high table has to look the other way; away from you, away from me. Something that hits where it hurts."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Landry Approach 3]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Approach 3
<<effects>>
<<He>> leans forward. "Instead of chasing small prizes with a handful of pills or a bit of cash, I'm talking about hitting the nerve centre. The bank itself."
<br><br>
<<if $speech_attitude is "meek">>
	"Rob a bank? I need some time to think about this," you say. Your heart is pounding.
<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
	"Rob a bank? Yeah, I'm going to need a minute with this one," you say. 
<<else>>
	"Rob a bank? I need some time," you say.
<</if>>
<br><br>
Landry nods slowly. "Take the time you need. But don't take too long.
<<if $xchange.blackmail.intro is 1>>"<span class="red">The high table doesn't wait for anyone</span>.<<else>>"<span class="elk">Their web gets tighter every day</span>.<</if>>
So, at least, you should know the details first."
<br><br>
"...Fine." You sigh.
<br><br>
<<link [[You're insane|Heist Landry React Insane]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[I'm listening|Heist Landry React Interested]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Stay silent|Heist Landry React Silent]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry React Insane
<<effects>>
<<if $speech_attitude is "meek">>
	"Still, that's... that's insane," you stammer. "You can't just rob a bank. Especially not that bank."
<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
	"Still, you're out of your mind," you say flatly. "Rob the one controlled by the scary invisible man? Brilliant plan."
<<else>>
	"Still, you're insane," you say. "That bank is a fortress."
<</if>>
<br><br>
Landry chuckles, a dry, humourless sound. "I didn't say it would be easy. I said it would be worth it. There's a difference."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Landry Explain]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry React Interested
<<effects>>
<<if $speech_attitude is "meek">>
	"I'm... I'm listening," you say carefully.
<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
	"Alright, I'll bite. What's the play?"
<<else>>
	"I'm listening," you say, meeting <<his>> gaze steadily.
<</if>>
<br><br>
Landry nods. "Good. I was hoping you'd say that."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Landry Explain]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry React Silent
<<effects>>
You say nothing. Landry watches you for a long moment, reading your silence.
<br><br>
"I'll take that as 'I'm terrified but curious,'" <<he>> says. <<if $speech_attitude is "bratty">>"Or maybe 'I think you're an idiot.' Either way, hear me out."<<else>>"Fair enough. Hear me out."<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Landry Explain]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Explain
<<effects>>
"Here's what I know," Landry begins. "The bank operates on two levels. Above ground, it's a normal financial institution. Tellers, accounts, the works.
But below, the underground, there's a vault system that handles the real business. Laundered money, pill distribution logistics, records of every operation the master runs in the city."
<br><br>
<<He>> traces an invisible layout on the table with <<his>> finger.
<br><br>
"The security is sophisticated. Cameras, coded locks, private guards... not the kind who call the police. The kind who make problems disappear." 
<br><br>
<<He>> meets your eyes. "But no system is perfect. There are gaps. Shift changes, blind spots, human error. You just need to know where to look."
<br><br>
<<He>> sits back. "That's where the problem is. I don't know where to look. I don't have the skills for it. But I know someone who might."
<br><br>
<<set $xchange.bankHeist.landryWarned to true>>
<<if $wrenSeen?.length>>
	<<link [[Wren|Heist Landry Wren Known]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<link [[Who?|Heist Landry Wren Unknown]]>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Heist Landry Wren Known
<<effects>>
<<if $speech_attitude is "meek">>
	"You mean Wren, don't you?" you say quietly.
<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
	"Let me guess... hm, Wren." You almost smile. "The smuggler with an ego problem."
<<else>>
	"Wren," you say. It's not a question.
<</if>>
<br><br>
Landry raises <<his>> eyebrows, genuinely surprised. "You know <<nnpc_him "Wren">>? Well. That saves me some trouble."
<br><br>
<<He>> leans forward. "Then you know <<nnpc_hes "Wren">> resourceful, clever, and just reckless enough to consider something like this.
Go to <<nnpc_him "Wren">>. Explain what we're planning. If <<nnpc_he "Wren">> agrees to help, come back and we'll work out the details."
<br><br>
<span class="green"><i>You can now approach Wren about the heist.</i></span><br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Pub]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Wren Unknown
<<effects>>
"Who?" you ask.
<br><br>
"A smuggler. Goes by Wren. Operates out of the docks, mostly. Runs goods through the canal system under the city." Landry scratches <<his>> chin. 
"Sharp mind. Nimble fingers. Exactly the sort of person you need for something like this."
<br><br>
<<He>> gives you a considering look. "Finding <<nnpc_him "Wren">> might take some doing. <<nnpc_Hes "Wren">> not the type to advertise."
<br><br>
<<He>> ticks off options on <<his>> fingers. "The docks is your best bet. <<nnpc_He "Wren">> sometimes surfaces at night near the old warehouses. 
Keep your eyes open and your mouth shut, and you'll cross paths eventually."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Landry Wren Unknown 2]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Wren Unknown 2
<<effects>>
<<if $speech_attitude is "meek">>
	"That's not very specific," you say nervously.
	<br><br>
	"It's specific enough," <<he>> replies. "Wren doesn't get found. Wren finds you. Just make sure you're in the right places."
<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
	"Great. A scavenger hunt," you mutter.
	<br><br>
	Landry smirks. "Consider it a test. If you can't find one smuggler, you've no business robbing a bank."
<<else>>
	You nod. It's vague, but you've worked with less.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<set $xchange.bankHeist.wrenHintGiven to true>>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Pub]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Wren Hint
<<endevent>>
<<effects>><<npc Landry>><<person1>>
<<if $speech_attitude is "meek">>
	"I haven't been able to find Wren yet," you admit.
<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
	"Your smuggler friend is pretty elusive. Any better hints?"
<<else>>
	"I still need to find Wren. Anything else you can tell me?"
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<if !$wrenSeen?.length>>
	Landry scratches <<his>> jaw. "Try the canal late in the day. <<nnpc_He "Wren">> moves product around dusk. 
	If the weather's bad, <<nnpc_he "Wren">> sometimes holes up near the warehouses on the industrial estate."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> pauses thoughtfully. "<<nnpc_Hes "Wren">> cautious, but not paranoid. Just be patient."
<<else>>
	Landry gives you a flat look. "You've met <<nnpc_him "Wren">> before. You know <<nnpc_his "Wren">> haunts. 
	Stop overthinking it and go talk to <<nnpc_him "Wren">>."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Pub]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Mickey Mapping
<<endevent>>
<<effects>><<npc Landry>><<person1>>
<<if $speech_attitude is "meek">>
	"Wren sent me," you say. "The mapping is done. <<nnpc_He "Wren">> said to bring it to... your friend."
<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
	"Special delivery from Wren." You glance at the door to Mickey's room. "Your little hacker friend in?"
<<else>>
	"The mapping is done. Wren said to bring it here for your friend to look at."
<</if>>
<br><br>
Landry nods and raps twice on Mickey's door. "Got something for you."
<br><br>
The door cracks open. Mickey's eyes peer through the gap. They spot the papers in your hand and the door opens wider.
"These the bank layouts?" 
<br><br>
You nod. They snatch the papers from your hand and disappear back inside. You hear them spread the pages across a surface, muttering to themselves.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Landry Mickey Mapping 2]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Mickey Mapping 2
<<effects>>
A minute passes. Then two. Landry drums <<his>> fingers on the table.
<br><br>
Mickey's voice comes through the door. "Magnetic strip readers on the service level. Camera system runs on a local network, not hardwired. The vault level..." 
<br><br>
A pause. More muttering. 
<br><br>
"The vault level has its own isolated power and security loop. Old but solid."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Landry Mickey Mapping 3]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Mickey Mapping 3
<<effects>>
The door opens again. Mickey leans against the frame, arms crossed.
<br><br>
"I can kill the camera feed for the service level remotely. Thirty-second blackout, timed to your shift change window. That gives you and Wren clean passage to the vault staircase." 
They tap the doorframe. "The vault itself, I can't touch from here. That's on you and your skills."
<br><br>
<<if $skulduggery gte 600>>
	"But with what I'm seeing in these layouts, you should be fine," they add. "Good-good."
<<elseif $skulduggery gte 400>>
	"It'll be tight," they say. "But doable, if you don't panic."
<<else>>
	They look at you for a long moment. "You're going to want to sharpen up before you go in there. The vault won't be forgiving."
<</if>>
<br><br>
Mickey retreats and the door clicks shut. You hear the sound of a complex lock setting into place.
<br><br>
<<set $xchange.bankHeist.heistReady to true>><<set $xchange.bankHeist.mickeyPrepDay to Time.days>><<set $xchange.bankHeist.mickeyPrepDays to random(3, 7)>>
Landry turns back to you. "Sounds like we're as ready as we'll ever be. Come talk to me when you want to set a date."
<br><br>
<span class="green"><i>The heist is ready. Talk to Landry to begin.</i></span>
<br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Pub]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Report
<<endevent>>
<<effects>><<npc Landry>><<person1>><<wearProp "keycard" "black">>
You find Landry in <<his>> usual spot, but <<he>> doesn't look relaxed. <<He>> catches sight of you and straightens immediately.
<br><br>
<<if $speech_attitude is "meek">>
	"It's done," you say. Your hands are still trembling slightly.
<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
	You toss something onto the table. A card, plain and dark. "Miss me?"
<<else>>
	"It's done," you say, sliding into the booth across from <<him>>.
<</if>>
<<if $speech_attitude isnot "bratty">>
	<br><br>
	You produce the card you cloned from the vault terminal. Landry stares at it, then at you.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Landry Report 2]]>><<handheldon>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Report 2
<<effects>>
"<<pShe>> actually did it," Landry breathes. 
<br><br>
For a moment, <<he>> looks genuinely stunned. Then <<he>> grins, the first real smile you've seen from <<him>>.
<br><br>
"You beautiful lunatic. You actually pulled it off!" <<He>> picks up the card, turning it over in <<his>> fingers.
"Do you know what this is? This is a skeleton key. Every account the master runs through that bank, this card can access them. Track them. See where the money flows."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Landry Report Mickey]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Report Mickey
<<effects>>
A door cracks open behind you.
<br><br>
Mickey is already halfway across the pub before Landry can react. They move fast, faster than you'd have guessed for someone who spends all day behind a locked door. 
Their eyes are fixed on the card in Landry's hand.
<br><br>
They snatch it. Clean. One motion. Landry barely has time to blink.
<br><br>
"What the..." Landry starts, half-rising from <<his>> seat. <<He>> glances between you and Mickey, then at the other patrons, already moving to block their line of sight. 
"Mickey, get back in your room. People can see you."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Landry Report Mickey 2]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Report Mickey 2
<<effects>>
Mickey isn't listening. They turn the card over in their hands, holding it up to the dim pub light. Their eyes narrow. Their lips move, reading something invisible on the surface.
<br><br>
"This is the real thing," they mutter. "Do you know what this is?"
<br><br>
"That's what I was just explaining, if you'd..." Landry trails off.
<br><br>
"Shut up." Mickey doesn't even look at <<him>>. They're already walking back towards their room, card in hand. "I'm keeping this."
<br><br>
Landry stares after them, mouth open.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Landry Report Mickey 3]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Report Mickey 3
<<effects>>
Mickey pauses at the door to their room and turns back to you. Their expression is different now. Focused, but not unkind.
<br><br>
"That card is raw access credentials. Useless to you as-is. You'd get flagged and frozen within a day." They tap the card against the doorframe. 
"But I can use it. As exchange... I will give you <i>a proper card</i>."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Landry Report Mickey 4]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Report Mickey 4
<<effects>><<wearProp "keycard" "black">>
<<run setup.hbsc.ensureState()>>
<<if $hbsc.account.level gte 1>>
	"You already have a bank account, yeah? Good-good." They disappear into their room. You hear rapid typing. A pause. More typing.
	<br><br>
	They lean back out, holding a different card. Sleek. Black. Your name on it.
	<br><br>
	"Your existing account just got bumped to <span class="gold">Black tier</span>. No minimum balance requirement, no questions asked. 
	As far as the bank's system is concerned, you've always been a Black client." They toss you the card. "Don't thank me. Thank whoever built their security this badly."
<<else>>
	"You don't have a bank account." It's not a question. "Good-good. That actually makes this easier."
	<br><br>
	They disappear into their room. You hear rapid typing. A pause. More typing.
	<br><br>
	They lean back out, holding a card. Sleek. Black. Your name on it.
	<br><br>
	"<span class="gold">Black tier savings account</span>. Opened, verified, clean as a whistle. 
	As far as the bank's system knows, you've been a client for years." They toss you the card. "Don't thank me. Thank whoever built their security this badly."
<</if>>
<<set $hbsc.account.level to 5>><<set $xchange.bankHeist.blackCardObtained to true>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Landry Report Mickey 5]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Report Mickey 5
<<effects>>
<<if $speech_attitude is "meek">>
	"Thank you," you say, a little overwhelmed.
	<br><br>
	"I just said don't thank me." The door clicks shut. You hear the sound of a complex lock setting into place.
<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
	"So you can do more than lurk behind that door," you say.
	<br><br>
	"And you can do more than pick locks. We're both full of surprises." The door clicks shut. You hear the sound of a complex lock setting into place.
<<else>>
	You catch the card. Mickey nods once and shuts the door. You hear the sound of a complex lock setting into place.
<</if>>
<br><br>
You turn back to Landry. <<He>> looks like <<hes>> still processing what just happened.
<br><br>
"Well," <<he>> says after a moment. "That went... differently than I expected." <<He>> shakes <<his>> head and pushes a small wrapped package across the table. 
"Got something for you too, as my own <i>thank you</i>. <span class="gold">Premium pills. Three of them.</span> Pulled from a different supply line than Briar."
<<set $xchange.bankHeist.premiumPillsReceived to true>>
<<set $world_corruption_hard -= 1>>
<<set $sexStats.pills.pills["X-Change Premium"].owned += 3>>
<<set $xchange.premium.ownedBase to $sexStats.pills.pills["X-Change Premium"].owned>>
<<set $xchange.premium.doseBase to $sexStats.pills.pills["X-Change Premium"].doseTaken>>
<br><br><<earnFeat "Grand Theft Auto">>
<<link [[Tell Landry about the figure you saw|Heist Landry Report Master]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Keep the figure to yourself|Heist Landry Report Silent]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Report Master
<<effects>>
<<if $speech_attitude is "meek">>
	"There was... someone there," you say. "At the end. Watching me.
<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
	"One more thing. I wasn't alone down there. Someone was watching me. Something.
<<else>>
	"I saw someone," you say carefully. "As I was leaving. A figure.
<</if>>
They had..." You struggle for the words. "Antlers."
<br><br>
The colour drains from Landry's face. <<His>> grin vanishes.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Landry Report Master 2]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Report Master 2
<<effects>>
"Antlers." Landry's knuckles whiten around <<his>> glass. "Silver-tipped?"
<br><br>
You nod.
<br><br>
Landry is silent for a long time. When <<he>> speaks again, <<his>> voice is careful. The way someone talks when they're trying very hard not to be afraid.
"Then let you go. You understand that, don't you? You didn't escape. You didn't outsmart the security. <span class="elk">That</span>... watched you take what you took, and chose not to stop you."
<br><br>
<<He>> looks at the card in <<his>> hands.
<br><br>
"Which means either you've been given a gift," <<he>> says slowly, "or you've been given a leash."
<br><br>
<<set $xchange.bankHeist.landryReported to true>>
<<link [[Ask what to do then|Heist Landry Next]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Report Silent
<<effects>>
You decide to keep the figure to yourself. Some things are better left unsaid.
<br><br>
"Clean job. In and out," you say instead.
<br><br>
Landry nods, still grinning. "Beautiful. This changes things. This changes a lot of things." <<He>> settles back, more at ease than you've ever seen <<him>>.
<<He>> raises <<his>> glass. "To the beginning of the end."
<br><br>
But something nags at you. The memory of that figure. The antlers. The silver-tipped tendrils. The stillness.
<span class="navy">You can't shake the feeling that your success was permitted, not earned.</span>
<br><br>
<<set $xchange.bankHeist.landryReported to true>>
<<link [[Ask what comes next|Heist Landry Next]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Next
<<effects>>
"What now?" you ask.
<br><br>
Landry drums <<his>> fingers on the table, thinking.
<br><br>
"Now we use what Mickey pulled from the card. They can start mapping the operation, who gets paid, who moves the product, where the weak points are."
<br><br>
<<He>> pauses, expression growing serious.
<br><br>
"We are busy, and you... you've done enough. Get some rest."
<br><br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Pub]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
